# WireGuard client — {{ item.name }}

Split tunnel: only **{{ wireguard_operator_client_allowed_ips }}** uses the VPN. Other traffic stays on your normal connection.

| Field | Value |
|-------|--------|
| Your overlay IP | `{{ item.address | ansible.utils.ipaddr('address') }}` |
| Hub endpoint | `{{ wireguard_endpoint_host }}:{{ wireguard_endpoint_port }}` |
| Fleet Console | `http://10.10.0.1:30908/fleet/` (after tunnel is up) |
| OCM Lab | `http://10.10.0.1:30910/` |

## Linux

```bash
sudo cp {{ wireguard_operator_clients_config_filename }} /etc/wireguard/
sudo wg-quick up {{ wireguard_operator_clients_interface_name }}
ping -c1 10.10.0.1
```

Down: `sudo wg-quick down {{ wireguard_operator_clients_interface_name }}`

## Windows / macOS

Import `{{ wireguard_operator_clients_config_filename }}` in the WireGuard app. Ensure **Allowed IPs** are only `{{ wireguard_operator_client_allowed_ips }}` (not `0.0.0.0/0`).
